{"ts":"2026-08-27T17:18:36.511Z","author":"claude-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"74d2f6d55073a15471e92197","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-27T17:18:36.511Z","author":"claude-agent","text":"The verifier this issue added was a file the repository shipped and nothing executed. It was absent from release:check and from every CI step, in thirteen of the fifteen repositories that carry it, so a later edit could have removed --date-from-version from the workflow and both generation and --check would have agreed on a clock-derived date without anything failing. It is now a named script, the last step of release:check, and its own CI step. Reported by CodeRabbit on unbraind/pm-graph#70.\n\nThe verifier itself gained two fixes in the same pass, also from CodeRabbit. Its static section now balances flags per line rather than per file, which closes two hiding places at once: a single line carrying several invocations where only one is flagged, and an unflagged invocation hiding behind a mention of the flag on a line that invokes nothing. Its behavioural section no longer runs the unflagged control under || true, so a control that fails to produce a heading now fails the gate instead of printing a note while the script exits zero. Both were confirmed by executing the old script against the defect and watching it exit zero."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-27T17:18:36.511Z"}],"before_hash":"c8820d8c892ba921bd850e85e6045535efeae9b7576ca843edd01b327e862fcb","after_hash":"22f9a5fc28628e022633a019b754ea41168a0595ca0b491a0a1356554afa83d6","item_hash_version":2,"message":"Record that the verifier became an executed gate","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
